1. Install Docker Desktop
2. In project root run docker-compose up --build (takes several minutes)
3. Create django migrations and create superuser
4. docker-compose exec backend python manage.py migrate
5. docker-compose exec backend python manage.py createsuperuser
6. Django superuser username#password: Stranger#drunk
7. Start all services (detached): docker-compose up -d
8. Start already-created containers (no recreate): docker-compose start
9. Stop containers: docker-compose stop
10. Stop & remove containers/networks (clean): docker-compose down
11. To start frontend npm start
12. On code or dependencies changes docker-compose up --build frontend(for specific service)
13. Qeueing through RabbitMQ. username#password: rabbit#rabbit


